# F2, the controller and compatibility consumers of the wave-2 display accessors (l10n/README.md). tests/run.sh
# compiles every path listed in tests/l10n/*.sources and runs each tests/l10n/**Test.java from the repository root.
# G5: the display accessors F2 switches to print the English ids they replace, and keep them as english(),
# pinned before the batch. It reuses ControlsEnglishTest's variant and descriptor lists (tests/l10n/b4.sources).
tests/l10n/characterization/ControllerConsumersTextTest.java
# G5: the observation question's English, and the English ids its callers pass it (featureValue, d.label).
tests/l10n/characterization/CompatQuestionTextTest.java
# F2 behaviour: the consumers show the display text under another source and keep the English ids (data, logs).
tests/l10n/ControllerConsumersTest.java
# F2 key names: the three keys follow the key rule and live in strings_compat.xml (no batch name).
tests/l10n/CompatKeyNamesTest.java
